From f5671b2ea625cd41942404d291205de1f523279f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pooya Parsa <pooya@pi0.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:17:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: clear the exclusive monitor on every return to user
 mode

On arm64 an exception return (ERET) clears the local exclusive monitor,
so an STXR after a syscall, a fault, an interrupt or a task switch
fails, whatever ran in between; qemu-user does the same. kwemu's monitor
belongs to the CPU, and the kernel closed it only at a task switch,
signal delivery and sigreturn, so LDXR; SVC; STXR passed here.

Close it in user_mode_loop() before each kw_run(), which is every entry
to user mode. A loop of LDXR and STXR that a slice end interrupts fails
once and retries, as on hardware.
---
 arch/wasm/kernel/traps.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/wasm/kernel/traps.c b/arch/wasm/kernel/traps.c
index 7587e52e17f..b9a22f81e9b 100644
--- a/arch/wasm/kernel/traps.c
+++ b/arch/wasm/kernel/traps.c
@@ -141,6 +141,14 @@ void __noreturn user_mode_loop(struct pt_regs *regs)
 		if (unlikely(READ_ONCE(kw_park_users)))
 			kw_park_user();
 
+		/*
+		 * Each entry to user mode is an exception return, and on arm64
+		 * ERET clears the local exclusive monitor (qemu-user does the
+		 * same): an STXR after a syscall, a fault, an interrupt or a
+		 * task switch fails, whatever the kernel ran meanwhile.
+		 */
+		kw_clear_reservation(cpu);
+
 		/*
 		 * "sret": user mode runs with interrupts enabled. On SMP without
 		 * taking what is pending here: kw_run() sees it at once
-- 
